WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.194
Hi! Which is bigger, 452 or 425? Today we'll compare and order numbers, find number patterns, and sort odd and even numbers.

2
00:00:13.344 --> 00:00:19.074
First count the digits. A 3-digit number is bigger than a 2-digit number.

3
00:00:19.224 --> 00:00:23.298
With the same number of digits, compare the hundreds first.

4
00:00:23.448 --> 00:00:31.362
Both have 4 hundreds. Compare the tens: 5 is more than 2, so 452 is bigger.

5
00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:37.314
To order numbers, find the smallest first, then go one by one.

6
00:00:37.464 --> 00:00:42.786
Find the pattern: it goes up by 50 each time, so next is 300.

7
00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:47.322
First see if the numbers go up or down, then work out the difference.

8
00:00:47.472 --> 00:00:52.290
Numbers ending in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8 are even.

9
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:58.578
Numbers ending in 1, 3, 5, 7 or 9 are odd.

10
00:00:58.728 --> 00:01:06.234
Watch out! Don't just look at the ones and say 425 is bigger because 5 is more than 2!

11
00:01:06.384 --> 00:01:11.298
The hundreds are both 4, so compare the tens: 2 is less than 5.

12
00:01:11.448 --> 00:01:17.130
So 425 is smaller than 452.

13
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:29.778
Your turn! 638 or 683, which is bigger? Greater than or less than? Pause and think.

14
00:01:29.928 --> 00:01:40.890
Same hundreds; 3 tens is less than 8 tens, so 638 is less than 683. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:52.842
Another one! Order 507, 570 and 75 from biggest to smallest. Pause and think.

16
00:01:52.992 --> 00:02:07.938
75 has only 2 digits, so it's smallest. 570 is bigger than 507. So: 570, 507, 75. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:08.088 --> 00:02:18.618
Here's another! 800, 700, 600. What comes next? Pause and think.

18
00:02:18.768 --> 00:02:26.202
It goes down by 100 each time, so next is 500. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:26.352 --> 00:02:35.538
Try one more! Is 365 odd or even? Pause and think.

20
00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:41.106
It ends in 5, so it's odd. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:41.256 --> 00:02:49.914
Last one! What is the biggest 3-digit even number? Pause and think.

22
00:02:50.064 --> 00:03:01.362
The biggest 3-digit number is 999, which is odd. One less is 998, which is even. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:01.512 --> 00:03:11.658
Remember: compare by digits first, then from the hundreds. For patterns, see if numbers go up or down. The ones digit tells odd or even.

24
00:03:11.808 --> 00:03:17.082
Look at your house number today. Is it odd or even?

